INT. CAR WASH CONTROL ROOM - NIGHT

Cinderblock. Buzzing fluorescents. Soap suds crawl down a window. Beyond it, a dark tunnel of brushes, still.

NADIA ROSTOVA-BELL, 30s, courier jacket, sits on an overturned crate. A phone in her hand. A duffel at her feet.

She presses play.

NADIA (V.O.)
(recorded, steady)
Memo one. Tuesday. If you hear this, the handoff went fine.

Nadia winces.

NADIA (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Package is in the blue duffel. Do not open it.

She looks at the duffel. Doesn't move.

NADIA (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Memo two. Wednesday. Someone followed me from the depot.

She pauses it. Breathes. Presses again.

NADIA (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(recorded, thinner)
Memo three. They know the car wash. I don't know how.

Nadia stands. Checks the door. The deadbolt. The window. The tunnel.

A drip. A distant clank.

She freezes.

Nothing.

She sits again.

NADIA (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(recorded)
Memo four. I'm going to open the duffel. Whoever you are, I'm sorry.

Nadia stares at the phone.

NADIA
(whisper)
I never recorded this one.

She scrolls. The memo is dated tomorrow.

The voice continues, gentler.

NADIA (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(recorded)
It's just a hard drive. It's always been just a hard drive. Walk away.

Nadia lifts the duffel. Unzips it. A small black drive, a Post-it: "SORRY."

She laughs. Short. Hollow. Then not.

She pockets the drive. Shoulders the duffel.

At the door she hesitates. Presses delete.

NADIA (CONT'D)
(to the phone)
Memo five.

She exits. The brushes begin to spin behind her.
